// total_value(qty, px): the sum of qty[i] * px[i]
// Pass both vectors so that nothing is copied
// and neither can be changed.

widget.solution:
#include <vector>

double total_value(const std::vector<double>& qty, const std::vector<double>& px) {
    double total = 0;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < qty.size(); ++i)
        total += qty[i] * px[i];
    return total;
}

screens.prose:
A colleague wants weights that add up to 1. Their function works on its own copy without anyone noticing.

```cpp
void normalise(std::vector<double> w) {
    double sum = 0;
    for (double x : w) sum += x;
    for (double& x : w) x /= sum;
}

std::vector<double> w{2.0, 3.0, 5.0};
normalise(w);
std::cout << w[0] << "\n";
```

